<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi>Component Bags

A component bag is a dedicated container for crafting materials,
worn in the <ansi fg="yellow">Components</ansi> equipment slot.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ How It Works ━━━</ansi>

When you have a component bag equipped, crafting materials
automatically go into it when you pick them up or buy them.
The bag has a limited capacity and reduces the effective weight
of its contents.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Commands ━━━</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">sort</ansi>       Move loose materials from backpack into bag.
  <ansi fg="command">inventory</ansi>  Shows bag contents in the Components section.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Available Bags ━━━</ansi>

  <ansi fg="itemname">Component Pouch</ansi>       20 items, 30% weight reduction.
    Buy from Weaver Maren in Thornwall.

  <ansi fg="itemname">Artisan's Satchel</ansi>     40 items, 35% weight reduction.
    Tailoring recipe (skill 15).

  <ansi fg="itemname">Master's Component Case</ansi> 75 items, 45% weight reduction.
    Tailoring recipe (skill 30).

Removing the bag spills its contents back into your backpack.

<ansi fg="magenta-bold">See also:</ansi> <ansi fg="command">help sort</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help inventory</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help craft</ansi>
